=== stratify (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi stratify [OPTIONS] [PATH]...
Rank files from entrypoints and propose dependency-first numeric prefixes
e.g. ryi stratify --from src/main.ts --root . src/
Input: --entry <FILE> --depth <N> --root <DIR>
Flags: --pattern <GLOB> --from <PATH[:NAME][=RANK]> --base-lines <N> --kind <KIND>
stderr:
=== rename (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi rename [OPTIONS] [TARGET] [NEW]
Rename a symbol and every occurrence bound to it
e.g. ryi rename src/a.ts#slug slugged --root .
Input: --root <ROOT>
Flags: --list <LIST> --state <STATE> --at <AT> --verify-scip <INDEX>
Switches: --slow --commit --text-refs --no-scip-merge --json
stderr:
=== move (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi move [OPTIONS] [OLD] [NEW]
Move a file and repair every specifier that names it
e.g. ryi move src/a.ts src/b.ts --root .
Input: --root <ROOT>
Flags: --list <LIST> --verify-cwd <VERIFY_CWD> --state <STATE> --verify <VERIFY>
Switches: --commit --shim --relocate-mod --text-refs
stderr:
=== cleave (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Usage: ryi cleave [OPTIONS] [TARGET] [DEST]
Move one item into another file, with its imports
e.g. ryi cleave src/a.ts#slug src/slug.ts --root .
Input: --root <ROOT>
Flags: --list <LIST> --state <STATE> --verify <VERIFY>
Switches: --drag --slow --commit --text-refs --json
stderr:
